  "title": "A race condition during core updates that could lead to remote code execution",
  "summary": "During a core update that uses a complete package, WordPress extracted the new files to a predictable directory inside the web-served upgrade folder. An unauthenticated attacker who wins a race against that extraction could reach remote code execution.\r\n\r\nWordPress 7.1.4 has been released containing a fix for the vulnerability, and as a courtesy to users on older branches the fix has been backported to all branches back to 4.7.\r\n\r\nDiscovered and responsibly disclosed by [Umut Bayram](https://www.picussecurity.com/resource/author/umut-bayram).",
